<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="06">
<name>Brake</name>
<section id="1002J_S000U" variety="S000U">
<name>Brake Control</name>
<ttl id="1002J_S000U_744TG_T0089" variety="T0089">
<name>ABS with EBD &amp; TRC &amp; VSC &amp; BA System</name>
<para id="RM00000061200YX" category="J" type-id="8003H" name-id="442P3-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Actuator Initial Check Noise Is Loud</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000061200YX_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000061200YX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000061200YX_04_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___00007VA00000">
<testtitle>Road Test</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Compare the loudness of the noise generated when the vehicle first reaches 10km/h after the IG is turned ON with that of a vehicle of the same model.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Same or quieter</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the vehicle speed reaches 6km/h, the actuator initial check starts, so solenoid and motor operating noise is generated.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000061200YX_04_0011" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000061200YX_04_0008" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000061200YX_04_0008" proc-id="RM0550J___00007VB00000">
<testtitle>Adjust Actuator Assembly Installation</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Drain the brake fluid.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect all brake tubes from the actuator assembly. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000304V000X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the brake tubes so that the tension applied to the rubber mounts of the actuator assembly is even. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000304T000X"/>)</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>After connecting the brake tubes, add brake fluid and be sure to bleed the air. (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM000000DB000BX"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Relieving the tension applied to the brake tubes and rubber mounts may reduce the operating noise.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check whether the brake tubes interfere with the body or other parts.</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000061200YX_04_0009" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000061200YX_04_0009" proc-id="RM0550J___00007VC00000">
<testtitle>Reconfirm Symptom</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test and check the loudness of the operating noise again.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Same or quieter</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000061200YX_04_0012" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000061200YX_04_0010" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000061200YX_04_0010">
<testtitle>Replace ABS &amp; Traction Actuator Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000304V000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000061200YX_04_0011">
<testtitle>No Abnormality</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000061200YX_04_0012">
<testtitle>No Abnormality</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>